From b580463376787ba03c25de8766c5e879e12ab1e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: airidosas252 <airidaslideikis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:15:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/20] tu: add VK_KHR_ray_tracing_pipeline behind
 TU_EXPERIMENTAL=rt_pipeline

Ray tracing pipelines on A8XX, built on the existing ray query traversal
(also exposes VK_KHR_pipeline_library_group_handles). Shader group handles
are 32 bytes and maxRayRecursionDepth is 1. Trace rays, indirect and
indirect2 launches are supported.

The pipeline is compiled to one compute shader in one of three modes,
picked with TU_RT_MODE=monolithic,separate,aqe (add "log" to print how a
pipeline compiled):

- monolithic: hit, miss and callable shaders are inlined where they can
  run in each raygen shader.
- separate: every stage is a case of a scheduler loop with an explicit
  stack in private memory. This is the default for pipelines that are
  too big to inline.
- aqe: the stages are split into pieces that the kernel's AQE schedules,
  so it needs a kernel that enabled the AQE.

Also includes the small compiler support it needs: coherent ldg and
atomic.g for the AQE, splitting multi-dword ldp/stp so compute can keep the
per-wave private memory layout, and skipping triangles in ray queries.

Experimental: it passes the ray tracing pipeline CTS and small test apps,
but game-size pipelines don't work yet (hangs or very slow rendering, and
a lot of memory while compiling). Keep it behind TU_EXPERIMENTAL=rt_pipeline.
